# BoronDNS RPM package

The RPM installs static MUSL BoronDNS and BoronGun executables, creates the
`borondns` system account, and installs `borondns.service`. The service only
starts after `/etc/borondns-secondary/config.toml` exists.

Configuration and `/var/lib/borondns`, including the zone cache, are retained
when the package is removed. Delete operational data explicitly only when it is
no longer required.

Remove or migrate an archive installation and its locally managed
`/etc/systemd/system/borondns.service` before installing this RPM.

## Building a package

`scripts/package-rpm.sh` uses `workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml`.
GitHub tag refs, `BORONDNS_RELEASE_TAG`, and local release tags at HEAD must
match `vX.Y.Z` for that version when present. Pass `BORONDNS_RELEASE_TAG` when
building a source archive if you want to check its intended release tag.

`BORONDNS_RPM_VERSION`, if set, must match Cargo. Packaging-only revisions use
`BORONDNS_RPM_RELEASE`. Both input executables must run on the build host and
report the Cargo version with `--version`. Lifecycle tests use the same version
for their stubs, filenames, and installed-package assertions.
